From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:48:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: don't cancel a bus reset that was
 never set up

brcmf_alloc() sets bus_if->drvr at probe, but the bus_reset work is set
up only in brcmf_attach(), once the firmware has loaded. A remove or a
suspend in between cancels a work with no function, and __flush_work()
warns. brcmf_bus_schedule_reset() already checks for that: check in
brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work() as well.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index 1cda83068b..57f0a341f2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -1347,7 +1347,8 @@ void brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work(struct brcmf_bus *bus_if)
 {
 	mutex_lock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 	bus_if->removing = true;
-	if (bus_if->drvr)
+	/* Set up only by brcmf_attach(), once the firmware has loaded. */
+	if (bus_if->drvr && bus_if->drvr->bus_reset.func)
 		cancel_work_sync(&bus_if->drvr->bus_reset);
 	mutex_unlock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 }
